\name{cellucid_dataset_open}
\alias{cellucid_dataset_open}
\title{Open a dataset}
\usage{
cellucid_dataset_open(
  viewer,
  name,
  allocation = "proportional",
  count,
  embedding,
  field,
  fraction,
  kind = "any",
  method = NULL,
  seed = NULL
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{name}{A sample's name or id, a name from My datasets, a link to a dataset (a file, a Zarr store, a dataset folder, a CELLxGENE, Zenodo, Figshare or GitHub address), an accession (GSE123456, a DOI), or a Cellucid server (localhost:8765). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{allocation}{Stratified: how the cells are split over the categories. One of \code{"proportional"}, \code{"balanced"}. Default \code{"proportional"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{count}{How many cells, exactly (at least 2; the dataset's count or more opens every cell). Not with fraction. A whole number (at least 1). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{embedding}{Spatial: the obsm embedding it thins. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{field}{Stratified: the categorical column it is stratified by. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{fraction}{The share of the dataset's cells: 0.1 opens a tenth, 1 every cell. Not with count. A number (more than 0, at most 1). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{kind}{Where to look for the name: any (samples, then My datasets, then as a link), sample, my-datasets or link. One of \code{"any"}, \code{"sample"}, \code{"my-datasets"}, \code{"link"}. Default \code{"any"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{method}{How the cells are chosen; null for the file's default. One of \code{"uniform"}, \code{"blocks"}, \code{"stratified"}, \code{"spatial"}, \code{NULL}. Default \code{NULL}, the viewer's own.}
\item{seed}{The subsample's seed; null for the file's. A whole number or \code{NULL} (at least 0, at most 4294967295). Default \code{NULL}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{already_open} (It was open already, so nothing was opened again and its history goes on), \code{cells} (The cells open (a share of the dataset when it is subsampled)), \code{genes}, \code{kind} (Where it opens from: a built-in sample, a link, a Cellucid server, a file or folder of the person's computer, or a notebook (Python, R) that serves it), \code{name} (The dataset now open, as Cellucid names it), \code{saved_states} (Histories of this dataset kept in this browser from earlier visits; the person was offered to continue the latest), \code{total_cells}.
}
\description{
Open a dataset by the name the person gives: a built-in sample, one of their datasets (My datasets), a link, or an accession the link box takes. It replaces the open dataset; that one's history stays kept in this browser while Autosave keeps it (steps it does not keep are asked about first) and the new one starts its own. A link, accession or server the person has not typed, pasted or opened in this tab is asked of them first (before anything is requested), and so is a whole-file download. A count or fraction opens that subsample of its cells at once, read once (as cells_open takes it); without, it opens with the cells the person chose for openings (Session \ifelse{latex}{<U+203A>}{›} Subsampling), or the cells one of My datasets was last open with.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{dataset.open} (Datasets). It opens another dataset in place of the one the viewer shows, as an agent in the viewer does: it makes no step of the history.

A viewer opened from R shows the dataset R serves, so the viewer refuses this action from R: show another dataset with \code{\link{cellucid_view}}.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (large-download); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_dataset_open(viewer, name = "Pancreatic endocrinogenesis (scVelo)")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
